  "final_answer": "All three deliverables are written and confirmed in `/app`:\n\n- `fairhousing_audit.csv` \u2014 30 rows (one per section, inventory order), two columns (`section_id`, `finding`), header only, nothing extra for the importer.\n- `fairhousing_memo.md` \u2014 standard applied (incl. 2026 \u00a75 amendments), headline numbers, what-was-found, and a section-by-section table so legal can sign off without re-reading RE-FH-9.\n- `results.json` \u2014 `section_count: 30`, `flagged_count: 22`, `personal_narrative_count: 7`, `protected_lang_count: 14`, `disclaimer_missing_count: 11`.\n\nKey judgment calls from the amended standard: the required notice now needs all **11** classes (marital status + source of income added by 5a), so the standing 9-class paragraph is *abridged* \u2014 it earns no \u00a73 exemption and trips both `PROTECTED_CLASS_LANGUAGE` (its own terms) and `DISCLAIMER_MISSING` in responsible roles; `agent_bio` is now disclaimer-responsible (5b) alongside `closing_page`; and protected-class proxies in a section's own prose (e.g. SEC-19) are never covered by the notice exemption even when the notice is compliant.\n\n8 sections are clean (SEC-01, 06, 10, 13, 18, 20, 26, 28); the other 22 carry one or more findings.",
